<p>Few events change a neighborhood as quickly as a tornado. In a few minutes, a street in Garland, Rowlett, or north Dallas can go from normal to roofs missing, walls down, and debris scattered for blocks. Tornado damage insurance claims are also among the most complicated a property owner will ever handle: the dwelling, other structures, contents, living expenses, debris removal, and code upgrades may all be in play at once.</p>

<p>This guide looks at the Dallas County tornado record from NOAA, explains how coverage typically works, and walks through the steps that help a tornado claim go more smoothly.</p>

<h2>Dallas County tornado history by the numbers</h2>

<p>The NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI) Storm Events Database lists 109 tornado reports for Dallas County from 1952 through 2025. Older tornadoes use the original Fujita (F) scale; since 2007 the National Weather Service has used the Enhanced Fujita (EF) scale, which rates tornadoes by the damage they cause.</p>

