<p>About seven in ten Dallas County tornadoes were rated F0/EF0 or F1/EF1. Those weaker tornadoes still cause real claims: roofs stripped of shingles, fences flattened, trees through roofs, and broken windows. The stronger tornadoes are rarer, but they are responsible for the largest losses in the county's history.</p>

<h3>When tornadoes strike</h3>

<p>May (25 reports) and April (23) are the busiest months, followed by October (14) and March (13). The cool season matters more than many people expect: January has 10 reports and December has 9. Two of the most damaging tornadoes in recent Dallas history struck on December 26 and October 20.</p>

