<h3>December 26, 2015: Garland and Rowlett</h3>

<p>The EF4 tornado on the night after Christmas 2015 is the strongest in Dallas County since the 1994 Lancaster tornado. NOAA's narrative describes a path a little over 13 miles long, with nearly ten miles inside Dallas County. It began in Sunnyvale, crossed Interstate 30 at the President George Bush Turnpike, and continued through <a href="/service-areas/garland/">Garland</a> and <a href="/service-areas/rowlett/">Rowlett</a>. NOAA reports that the tornado affected nearly 600 homes in Dallas County and destroyed nearly 400 of them, along with 22 businesses. The same storm system produced a separate EF3 tornado that ended at the DeSoto and Glenn Heights city line.</p>

<h3>October 20, 2019: north Dallas</h3>

<p>On a Sunday night in October 2019, an EF3 tornado formed near State Highway 348 and Luna Road in northwest Dallas and tracked east-northeast. NOAA describes extensive damage to businesses and homes near Harry Hines Boulevard and Walnut Hill Lane, then significant roof damage to gas stations, large commercial buildings, churches, and at least one multi-story apartment complex as the tornado followed Walnut Hill Lane east. The same night, an EF2 tornado heavily damaged warehouses in Garland, including a newly built building whose concrete tilt-up walls collapsed, and an EF1 tornado damaged homes and outbuildings in Rowlett near the President George Bush Turnpike.</p>

<p>That storm is a reminder that Dallas tornado claims are not only residential. Retail centers, apartment complexes, schools, churches, and warehouses all filed claims, each with its own policy terms and business income questions.</p>

<h3>Smaller tornadoes, real claims</h3>

<p>Brief, weaker tornadoes are more common. On May 16, 2021, one supercell produced an EF0 tornado through Williams Park and Goar Park in <a href="/service-areas/highland-park/">Highland Park</a>, then an EF1 with 90 mph winds north of Royal Lane, where a home on Northaven Road had a partial roof collapse. On March 16, 2023, EF1 tornadoes damaged an auto dealership showroom in central <a href="/service-areas/irving/">Irving</a> and an apartment building on Shady Grove Road. Most of these losses look like severe wind claims, and they are handled the same way.</p>

